INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('2309-2', 'CEL Seminar - Dr. Soowon Chang from Purdue University', '/2309-2/', 'March 29th, 2022 10:00am – 11:30am Title: Transition of Energy Infrastructure Systems for Decarbonization Dr. Soowon Chang is an Assistant Professor and the Director of the Smart and Sustainable Human-Urban-Building (S2-HUB) Interaction Lab in the School of Construction Management Technology at Purdue University. She received her Ph.D. from Georgia Institute of Technology and conducted urban redevelopment research in Tokyo at the National Institute for Environmental Studies in Japan prior to joining Purdue. She received her B.S. in Architectural Engineering, B.A. in Management for Science and Technology, and M.S. in Architectural Engineering with emphasis on construction management from EWHA WOMANS UNIVERSITY in South Korea. Her research focuses on smart and sustainable building design and construction considering urban systems’ networks by modeling and simulation, functional and spatial optimization, cyber-physical interactions in smart cities. She served several international conferences in leadership capacities including technical committee, track chair, and session chair. Dr. Chang is an associate member of American Society of Civil Engineers. Zoom Link: https://snu-ac-kr.zoom.us/j/95174373244 Categories: NEWS 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 October 2019 July 2019 May 2019 March 2019 June 2017 Categories NEWS Principle Investigator / Publications Uncategorized Meta Log in Entries feed Comments feed WordPress.org');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('2313-2', 'CEL Seminar - Professor. Pengyang Wang from University of Macau', '/2313-2/', 'December 10th, 2021 15:30-16:30 Title: A Data-Driven Perspective for Intelligent Urban Planning Special lecture is happening by Professor Wang with the title of “A Data-Driven Perspective for Intelligent Urban Planning" Professor Pengyang Wang is an Assistant Professor in the State Key Lab of Smart Cities and Internet-of-Things at the University of Macau. His research interests are in data mining, machine learning and big data analytics, especially in representation learning for Spatial-Temporal Graph-Structured data, with applications to smart cities, transportation, user/system behavior modeling, critical infrastructure defense, and complex network analysis. Urban planning is an interdisciplinary and complex process that involves public policy, social science, engineering, architecture, landscape, and other related fields. Effective urban planning can help to mitigate the operational and social vulnerability of an urban system. Traditionally, such tasks are completed by professional planners. However, personal experiences and skills of planners are likely to bring biases as well as unreasonable operations into the plan solutions, which may raise severe issues in urban systems. The recent advance of big data and artificial intelligence motivates us to ask: “Can machines learn the hidden patterns of urban systems, and automatically generate data-driven urban plan solutions?” In this lecture, Professor Wang will introduce his recent work on automated intelligent urban planning. https://snu-ac-kr.zoom.us/j/81388233090?pwd=bzkxVHNKQVMvbExFSmo2cWpIdFk5UT09 Categories: NEWS 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 October 2019 July 2019 May 2019 March 2019 June 2017 Categories NEWS Principle Investigator / Publications Uncategorized Meta Log in Entries feed Comments feed WordPress.org');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('2316-2', 'CEL Seminar - Dr.Zhongming Shi', '/2316-2/', 'October 15th, 2021 11:00am – 12:00pm Title: Shaping cities: through science, by design Dr. Zhongming Shi is a postdoctoral researcher, principal investigator at the Future Cities Laboratory in Singapore. He obtained his Doctor of Sciences degree from ETH Zurich in 2020. He also holds degrees in architecture and urban design from China and United States. Zhongming’s doctoral research was on the topic of energy-driven urban design, which highlights the interdependencies between urban design and energy performance. Currently, he is on the development team of the Cities Knowledge Graph, a multi-domain master-planning support tool, and the City Energy Analyst, an urban building energy simulation tool. He is also leading a research project on building-integrated agriculture in Singapore. https://snu-ac-kr.zoom.us/j/85402256679 Categories: NEWS 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2