INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('2343-2', 'CEL Seminar - Dr. Kangkang Tong from Shanghai Jiao Tong University', '/2343-2/', '[GSES Environmental Planning and Design Guest Lecture 3] City Energy Lab welcomes everyone from GSES to join a guest lecture in the Environmental Planning and Design class. Speaker: Dr. Kangkang Tong from Shanghai Jiao Tong University Topic: Integrating Social Equity into Low Carbon Strategies in Cities Time: May 4th, 2022 14:00 - 15:00 Abstract: Cities are increasingly interested in advancing social equity in climate actions, such as reducing greenhouse gas emissions by reducing energy use. However, few comprehensive conceptual and data frameworks are available to address social inequality and equity in the energy sector at the fine intra-urban spatial scale in cities. This talk will introduce a framework for assessing social inequality and equity in energy sector. A specific application will be presented relating to energy use and intensity, that demonstrates approaches to unpack income and racial inequality in urban systems in two US cities. Short Bio: Kangkang (KK) Tong is an Assistant Professor at China-UK Low Carbon College, Shanghai Jiao Tong University. Her research is at the intersection of urban energy systems, climate change, and social equity. She is interested in exploring how urban systems contribute to carbon neutrality and social equity under ongoing energy transitions. Previously, she worked as a Post-doctoral Research Associate at Princeton University’s Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering and the University of Minnesota. Zoom Link: https://snu-ac-kr.zoom.us/j/99175036819 Contact: Sangkyo Jeong, skj5863@snu.ac.kr Categories: NEWS 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 October 2019 July 2019 May 2019 March 2019 June 2017 Categories NEWS Principle Investigator / Publications Uncategorized Meta Log in Entries feed Comments feed WordPress.org');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('2446-2', 'Urban Artificial Intelligence: Practice and Prospects', '/2446-2/', '[City Energy Lab Lecture] City Energy Lab welcomes everyone from GSES to join a guest lecture. Speaker: Prof. Xinyue Ye from Texas A&M University-College Station (TAMU) Topic: Urban Artificial Intelligence: Practice and Prospects Time: October 17th, 2022 11:00 AM - 12:00 PM Venue: Zoom Lecture Short Bio: Prof. Xinyue Ye is Fellow of American Association of Geographers (AAG) and Fellow of Royal Geographical Society (with IBG), holding Harold L. Adams Endowed Professorship in Department of Landscape Architecture and Urban Planning & Department of Geography at Texas A&M University-College Station (TAMU), USA. He directs the focus of transportation in the PhD program of Urban and Regional Science at TAMU, and is the Interim Director of Center for Housing and Urban Development. His research focuses on geospatial artificial intelligence, geographic information system, and smart cities. Prof. Ye won the national first-place research award from University Economic Development Association. He was the recipient of annual research awards from both computational science (New Jersey Institute of Technology) and Geography (Kent State University) as well as AAG Regional Development and Planning Distinguished Scholar Award. He was one of the top 10 young scientists named by The World Geospatial Developers Conference in 2021. His work has been funded by National Science Foundation, National Institute of Justice, Department of Commerce, Department of Energy, and Department of Transportation. Prof. Ye is Editor-in-Chief of Computational Urban Science, an open access journal published by Springer. He also serves as the co-editor of Journal of Planning Education and Research, the flagship journal of Association of Collegiate Schools of Planning. Categories: Uncategorized 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 October 2019 July 2019 May 2019 March 2019 June 2017 Categories NEWS Principle Investigator / Publications Uncategorized Meta Log in Entries feed Comments feed WordPress.org');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('3052-2', 'Roundtable at International conference on PLANNING FRONTIERS FOR URBAN SUSTAINABILITY，Shanghai', '/3052-2/', 'July 3nd, 2024 9:00 am - 5:30 pm Title: Roundtable at International conference on PLANNING FRONTIERS FOR URBAN SUSTAINABILITY On July 3, 2024, the "PLANNING FRONTIERS FOR URBAN SUSTAINABILITY" International Conference was grandly held at the School of Architecture and Urban Planning, Tongji University. The conference was organized by Professor Zhuo Jian, Professor Diao Mi, and Assistant Professor Liu Chao from the Department of Urban Planning. It invited internationally renowned experts and young scholars from both domestic and foreign institutions to engage in discussions focused on national strategies and cutting-edge issues in sustainable urban planning. The academic discussions were conducted through presentations and roundtable meetings, aiming to connect international knowledge and explore the future of planning education while promoting international exchange in the field of urban planning. The discussion focused on the theme of "Global Collaboration," exploring collaborative efforts and innovative strategies among global partners to address pressing urban sustainability challenges. Categories: NEWS 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 October 2019 July 2019 May 2019 March 2019 June 2017 Categories NEWS Principle Investigator / Publications Uncategorized Meta Log in Entries feed Comments feed WordPress.org');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('53rd-uaa-conference-vancouver-bc-canada', '53rd UAA conference, Vancouver, BC, Canada', '/53rd-uaa-conference-vancouver-bc-canada/', 'Apr 15th - Apr 19th, 2025 Title: 53rd UAA conference - Vancouver, BC, Canada Master''s student Yeonjoon Moon presented her work via the poster - ''Identify Urban Block Typology In Seoul Using Improved KMeans Clustering Method''. Master''s student Lili Lin presented her work -''Local climate zone and urban heat resilience – An empirical study in New York City''. Master''s student Yoojung Choi presented her work - ''Energy prediction, Machine Learning, sustainable development, environmental assessment''. Categories: Uncategorized 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 Octobe