INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('about-2-2', 'About', '/about-2-2/', 'Background In response to the pressing global challenges posed by rapid urbanization and climate change, cities find themselves compelled to make significant strides in energy efficiency, carbon reduction, and heat mitigation. Simultaneously, urban places are undergoing substantial transformations to adapt to the continually evolving spectrum of local development issues. This transformative period also opens doors to unprecedented opportunities propelled by the growth of big data, enhanced computational power, and advancements in artificial intelligence (AI), promising innovative solutions to address these concerns. The City Energy Lab is at the forefront of pioneering innovative urban analytics and urban design methodologies, tirelessly seeking better solutions that integrate environmental considerations (energy and climate) with the intricate tapestry of social and local issues in urban development within the global context. Our fundamental inquiries propel our research endeavors: • What is “good city form” in the era of climate change to address both global and local issues? • How to enhance urban planning and design processes for sustainable neighborhood and city development with advanced computational tools? • How to utilize big data and new urban analytics to establish sustainable zoning systems to better regulate urban development? Our research agenda unfolds through strategic imperatives: • Developing Urban Scale Energy and Climate Modeling. We are employing an interdisciplinary approach that integrates simulation and AI techniques to comprehensively simulate and reveal complex relationships within the urban environment, with a specific emphasis on building energy and urban climate. • Exploiting Machine Learning for Urban Form Representation. We are applying representational learning to identify typologies of urban form, considering both physical and social aspects, to better represent diverse urban environments. • Adopting AI-aided design (AIAD) to Support the Planning and Design Process. We are integrating scientific tools and AI techniques into the Smart Design approach, enhanced by AIAD, to support planning and design process, fostering the ideas of “science for design” and “design in science.” • Conducting Comparative Case Studies. We are examining the aforementioned research topics through comparative case studies in global cities with different social, cultural, and economic contexts, viewing cities as dynamic scientific laboratories to rigorously test the solutions addressing global and local challenges for sustainable urban development. In essence, the City Energy Lab is unwaveringly committed to pioneering transformative approaches grounded in scientific rigor and design thinking. We aspire to shape sustainable and resilient cities, adeptly navigating the complexities of unprecedented global changes and local challenges through innovative research and actionable solutions.');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('academic-exchange-shenzhen-urban-planning-land-resource-research-center-visits-the-city-energy-lab', '[Academic Exchange] Shenzhen Urban Planning & Land Resource Research Center Visits the City Energy Lab', '/academic-exchange-shenzhen-urban-planning-land-resource-research-center-visits-the-city-energy-lab/', 'Resentatives from the Planning and Natural Resources Bureau of Shenzhen Municipality visited the City Energy Lab for an academic exchange focused on current research and the future development of urban planning. During the visit, Professor Steven Jige Quan and the Shenzhen delegation delivered presentations introducing their respective research activities and perspectives. The Shenzhen presentation was titled “Urban Index of Shenzhen: Global Public Goods for Urban Governance.” Following the presentations, participants discussed future directions for urban planning, including new approaches to urban governance, research collaboration, and the role of data-driven methods in addressing complex urban challenges. The visit provided an opportunity to exchange knowledge, identify shared research interests, and strengthen academic connections between the two institutions. Categories: Uncategorized 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 October 2019 July 2019 May 2019 March 2019 June 2017 Categories NEWS Principle Investigator / Publications Uncategorized Meta Log in Entries feed Comments feed WordPress.org');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('academic-visit-aua-fellowship-visit-and-invited-talks-in-china', '[Invited Talks & Academic Exchange] AUA Fellowship Visit and Invited Talks in China', '/academic-visit-aua-fellowship-visit-and-invited-talks-in-china/', '[Visit Information] Program: Asia University Alliance (AUA) Fellowship Period: March 23–27, 2026 Activities: Academic meetings and invited lectures Highlight Professor Steven Jige Quan visited Tsinghua University through the support of the Asia University Alliance (AUA) Fellowship Program. During the visit, he met with scholars in urban planning, architecture, and environmental studies, while delivering invited talks at four major universities in China. Summary Between March 23 and 27, Professor Steven Jige Quan participated in an academic exchange visit hosted by Tsinghua University under the AUA Fellowship Program. During the visit, he engaged in interdisciplinary discussions with researchers and faculty members on AI-assisted urban design, sustainable urban systems, and environmental planning. As part of the visit, he delivered invited lectures at Tsinghua University, Peking University, Renmin University of China, and Beijing Jiaotong University. The talks introduced recent research from the City Energy Lab on artificial intelligence–assisted environmental planning and design, urban energy systems, and human-centered AI applications for sustainable cities. The visit further strengthened international academic collaboration and research exchange between Seoul National University and leading universities in China. Invited Talks Tsinghua University — School of Architecture Peking University — College of Urban and Environmental Sciences Renmin University of China — School of Public Administration Beijing Jiaotong University — School of Architecture and Design Keywords AUA Fellowship / International Collaboration / Invited Talks / AI-Assisted Design / Sustainable Cities Categories: Uncategorized 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 October 2019 July 2019 May 2019 March 2019 June 2017 Categories NEWS Principle Investigator / Publications Uncategorized Meta Log in Entries feed Comments feed WordPress.org');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('ai-and-cities-an-international-forum-for-innovation-and-collaboration', 'AI and Cities: An International Forum for Innovation and Collaboration', '/ai-and-cities-an-international-forum-for-innovation-and-collaboration/', '9th-10th, 2025 Professor Quan and lab members attended the conference. Professor Quan hosted the session 8-''LLM for Planning'' as the moderator, and presented ''Integrating large language models into participatory planning support systems-Amulti-agent platform for enhancing stakeholder engagement''. Yoojung Choi presented ''Energy Prediction, Machine Learning, Sustainable Development, Environmental Assessment '', won the Best Presentation/Research Award as part of the Student Awards. Congratulations! Lili Lin presented ''Assessing Urban Heat Resilience: Nonlinear Impacts of Urban Form Factors Across Scales Using Machine Learning''. Program Categories: Uncategorized 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 October 2019 July 2019 May 2019 March 2019 June 2017 Categories NEWS Principle Investigator / Publications Uncategorized Meta Log in Entries feed Comments feed WordPress.org');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('ai4cities-workshop-in-tongji-university-shanghai-china', 'AI4Cities workshop in Tongji University, Shanghai, China', '/ai4cities-workshop-in-tongji-university-shanghai-china/', 'July 7th – 13th, 2025 Led by Professor Quan and Professor Pengyang Wang, our lab students, Lili Lin and Sihyeon Kim, with Students from Macao University and Students from Tongji University, co-worked in the AI4Cities workshop and finished the work named ''Participatory Urban Regeneration Empowered by Artificial Intelligence'', which won the competition of ''Best cross-disciplinary Integration Award''. At the end of the ceremony, Professor Quan, as the representative of the committee, noted that during the week, mentors and global participants deeply explored the future of urban studies and AI integration, and were inspired by the participants'' strong passion for “AI + Cities,” reinforcing confidence in the AI4CITIES platform''s success https://upd-caup.tongji.edu.cn/6e/91/c36467a355985/page.htm Categories: Uncategorized 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 October 2019 July 2019 May 2019 March 2019 June 2017 Categories NEWS Principle Investigator / Publications Uncategorized Meta Log in Entries feed Comments feed WordPress.org');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('aiad-lecture-series-economic-analysis-and-data-analytics-applications-for-construction-engineering-and-project-management', 'AIDD Lecture Series - Economic Analysis and Data Analytics Applications for Construction Engineering and Project Management', '/aiad-lecture-series-economic-analysis-and-data-analytics-applications-for-construction-engineering-and-project-management/', 'June 21st, 2024 1:00 – 2:00 pm Title: Economic Analysis and Data Analytics Applications for Construction Engineering and Project Management Prof. Baabak Ashuri is Executive Director of the Professional Master''s in Occupational Safety and Health (PMOSH)Professor of Civil and Environmental Engineering, and Fellow of the Brook Byers Institute for Sustainable Systems(8B1SS) at Georgia Tech. Dr. Ashuri''s research has advanced theoretical foundations and applications in data analytics, economic decision analysis, and quantitative methods in infrastructure and construction engineering and his findings for enhancing the performance of infrastructure management, allowing other researchers to use operations in several subdomains directly related to construction decisions,e.g., artificial intelligence (Al) and design automation, alternative project delivery selection, and sustainable technology investments. Dr. Ashuri has 228 publications in these fields, including 77 refereed journal articles, 101 peer-reviewed conference papers, 47 research reports and guidebooks, 1 co-edited book, and 2 referred book chapters. Dr. Ashuri secured a funding amount of over $17M from the National Science Foundation (NSF), Federal HighwayAdministration (FHWA), Department of Energy (DOE), Build America Beurre (BAC), Georgia Department of Transportation (Georgia DOT)South Carolina Department of Transportation (SCDOT). Construction Industry Institute (CII), Royal Institution of Chartered Surveyors (RlCS), Southeast Transportation Consortium (STc), Louisiana Transportation Research Center(LTRC), Turner Construction, and Perkins + Will, to name a few. Dr. Ashuri received many awards including the American Society of Civil Engineers (ASCE) (Thomas Fitch Rowland paper award), the American Association of StateHighway and Transportation Officials(AASHTO) High-Value Research "Sweet Sixteen" Award, and the Design-BuildInstitute of America (DBlA) (Distinguished Leadership-Faculty). Dr. Ashuri has chaired the ASCE Construction Research Council (CRC) and served on the ASCE Construction Institute (Cl) Board of Governors. Categories: NEWS 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 October 2019 July 2019 May 2019 March 2019 June 2017 Categories NEWS Principle Investigator / Publications Uncategorized Meta Log in Entries feed Comments feed WordPress.org');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('aiad-lecture-series-sustainable-and-integrated-built-environments-for-decarbonization', 'AIDD Lecture Series - Sustainable and Integrated Built Environments for Decarbonization', '/aiad-lecture-series-sustainable-and-integrated-built-environments-for-decarbonization/', 'June 21st, 2024 2:00 - 3:00 pm Title: Sustainable and Integrated Built Environments for Decarbonization Soowon Chang is an Assistant Professor of Construction Management Technology at Purdue University. She received her Ph.D. in Building Construction from the Georgia InstituteofTechnology. During her doctoral studies, she conducted research on smart and sustainable Tokyo redevelopment at the NationaInstitute for Environmental Studies in Japan, She also serves as a Global Professor in the Graduate School of System Design and Management at Keio University, Japan, and as an Early Career Editorial Board Member for the Journal of sustainable cities and Society-Elsevier. With diverse background in management, and urban planning, she focuses on engineering architectural engineering, construction civil systems. She currently dedicates herself to integrating low-carbon efficient and decarbonized strategies across buildings and infrastructure networks, as well as utilizing generative Al approaches in research and education. As an educator, she is committed to fostering students’ professional and ethical awareness, as well as a lifelong learning attitude. At Purdue, she teaches a variety of courses, including computational Design Data and interoperability, Building Information Management (BlM), Sustainability Design, Construction, and Development, Building Energy Modeling, and Construction Management. Categories: NEWS 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 October 2019 July 2019 May 2019 March 2019 June 2017 Categories NEWS Principle Investigator / Publications Uncategorized Meta Log in Entries feed Comments feed WordPress.org');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('aiad-workshops-urban-heat-resilience-workshop', 'AIDD Workshops - Urban Heat Resilience Workshop', '/aiad-workshops-urban-heat-resilience-workshop/', 'June 7th, 2024 2:00 – 4:30 pm Title: Workshops on Urban Heat Resilience and the Application of Large Language Models in Urban Planning We are honored to invite Dr. Chaosu Li, Dr. Wei Wang, Dr. Xinyu Fu, Dr. Yingnan Li, and Professor Wen-syan Li from the School of Data Science as speakers and panelists for two workshops on Urban Heat Resilience and the application of large language models in urban planning. During the Urban Heat Resilience Workshop, Dr. Chaosu Li and Dr. Wei Wang presented their work, while Dr. Xinyu Fu and Dr. Yingnan Li participated as discussants, contributing to the engaging discussions. Dr. Chaosu Li – Exposure and Resilience to Extreme Heat Events. Dr. Chaosu Li is an assistant professor of urban planning at the Urban Governance and Design Thrust of the Hong Kong University of Science and Technology(Guangzhou). He received his Ph.D.in City and Regional Planning from the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill (uNC-chapel Hil. He has expertise in urban planning for climate change and urban big data analytics. His work has been published in the Journal of the American Planning Association (JAPA), Journal of Planning Education and Research (JPER), Environment and Planning A, Environment and Planning B, among others. Dr. Li''s research projects have been supported by the National Natural Science Foundation of China (NSFC), Macau Foundation, etc. Dr. Wei Wang – Urban and Infrastructure Design to Respond to Urban Heat Resilience Dr. Wei Wang is an associate professor at the School of Architecture, Southeast University, Nanjing, Jiangsu province, China. His research areas mainly focus on sustainable urban design, urban building energy model, and resilient urban system. During the Application of Large Language Models in Urban Planning Workshop, Dr. Xinyu Fu presented his work, while Dr. Wen-Syan Li and Dr. Chaosu Li participated as discussants, contributing to the engaging discussions. During the Application of Large Language Models in Urban Planning Workshop, Dr. Xinyu Fu presented his work, while Dr. Wen-Syan Li and Dr. Chaosu Li participated as discussants, contributing to the engaging discussions. Dr. Xinyu Fu – Leveraging Large Language Models for Urban Planning Xinyu Fu is a senior lecturer of environmental planning at the University of Waikato, NewZealand. His current research interests center on flood risk management, agent-based modelling, and Al applications in planning. He has published over 30 research articles in top journals such as JAPA, JPL, Cities, and Urban Studies. Xinyu''s work is currently funded by theMBlE Endeavour Fund and EQC. Categories: NEWS 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 