bruary 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 October 2019 July 2019 May 2019 March 2019 June 2017 Categories NEWS Principle Investigator / Publications Uncategorized Meta Log in Entries feed Comments feed WordPress.org');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('cel-seminar-charging-towards-sustainability-future-ev-charging-stations', 'CEL Seminar - Charging Towards Sustainability: Future EV Charging Stations', '/cel-seminar-charging-towards-sustainability-future-ev-charging-stations/', 'May 8th, 2024 4:00pm Title: Charging Towards Sustainability: Future EV Charging Stations Heejung Yim, a research director of sustainability at the Stanford Center in Korea, works for various aspects of sustainability, particularly focusing on the circular economy in urban areas and the dynamics of energy transition markets. Her research interests extend to renewable energy markets, associated technologies, and urban green infrastructure. Heejung brings extensive professional experience to her role. She has worked as a management consultant at Nomura Research Institute America, IBM Consulting, and PWC Consulting Korea. She has also contributed her expertise to several startups in both Korea and the United States, including her own venture. She holds a master''s degree in sustainability from Columbia University and a bachelor''s degree in history and business administration from Sogang University. Categories: Uncategorized 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 October 2019 July 2019 May 2019 March 2019 June 2017 Categories NEWS Principle Investigator / Publications Uncategorized Meta Log in Entries feed Comments feed WordPress.org');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('cel-seminar-dr-jianxiang-huang-from-university-of-hongkong', 'CEL Seminar – Dr. Jianxiang Huang from University of Hongkong', '/cel-seminar-dr-jianxiang-huang-from-university-of-hongkong/', '[GSES Environmental Planning and Design Guest Lecture 5] City Energy Lab welcomes everyone from GSES to join a guest lecture in the Environmental Planning and Design class. Speaker: Dr. Jianxiang Huang from University of Hongkong Topic: Sustainable High-Density Cities - Evidence and Lessons from Hong Kong Time: May 18th, 2022 14:00 - 15:00 Short Bio: Jianxiang Huang is an assistant professor in the Department of Urban Planning and Design at the University of Hong Kong. He serves as the director of the Sustainable High Density Cities Lab, a multi-disciplinary research group. He has led many research projects on human behaviors and exposure to heat, noise, air pollutions, and infectious disease risks. He also studies the human-built environment interactions through the lens of “urban new data”, i.e., social media, POI, behavioral data, and wellbeing. He developed a series of design and planning software tools to assess urban heat island mitigation, building energy efficiency, traffic noise mitigation, and enhance of occupant thermal comfort. Software tools developed based on his research have been applied in real-world projects internationally. Jianxiang teaches the urban design and analytics curriculum at the University of Hong Kong. He is LEED accredited professional and a member of the American Institute of Certified Planners. Zoom Link: https://snu-ac-kr.zoom.us/j/96086027263 Contact: Sangkyo Jeong, skj5863@snu.ac.kr Categories: NEWS 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 October 2019 July 2019 May 2019 March 2019 June 2017 Categories NEWS Principle Investigator / Publications Uncategorized Meta Log in Entries feed Comments feed WordPress.org');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('cel-seminar-dr-longfeng-wu-from-peking', 'CEL Seminar - Dr. Longfeng Wu from Peking', '/cel-seminar-dr-longfeng-wu-from-peking/', '[GSES Environmental Planning and Design Guest Lecture 4] City Energy Lab welcomes everyone from GSES to join a guest lecture in the Environmental Planning and Design class. Speaker: Dr. Longfeng Wu from Peking University Topic: Environmental Justice and Urban Green Space - A Case of Beijing Time: May 11th, 2022 14:00 - 15:00 Short Bio: Longfeng Wu is an assistant professor (tenure-track) at Peking University, College of Urban and Environmental Sciences. His overarching research interest is about how to make sustainable and equitable urban environments. To achieve that, he is pursuing three multi-disciplinary topics: (1) social-spatial (in)equality of green/blue infrastructures and the driving factors, (2) public health outcomes of urban green spaces and the underlying mechanisms, and (3) land conservation in the light of climate change adaptation. His research incorporates mixed methods including data mining, GIS, social survey, spatial and statistical analyses, mapping, and visualization. Supported by more than 20 public/private research grants from Chinese Ministry of Education, Lincoln Institute of Land Policy and more, his research was published in several journals including Landscape and Urban Planning, Urban Studies, Environmental Science and Policy, Sustainable Cities and Societies, and Ecological Indicators. More importantly, his research aims to provide designers, planners, and decision-makers actionable information and ultimately promote more equitable and sustainable development for a neighborhood, a city, and a society at large. He was involved in several built urban green space projects in mainland China and, as a team leader, won more than 30 domestic/international urban planning and design competitions. Zoom Link: https://snu-ac-kr.zoom.us/j/99120322039 Contact: Sangkyo Jeong, skj5863@snu.ac.kr Categories: NEWS 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 October 2019 July 2019 May 2019 March 2019 June 2017 Categories NEWS Principle Investigator / Publications Uncategorized Meta Log in Entries feed Comments feed WordPress.org');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('cel-seminar-future-cities-through-science-by-design-in-place-over-time', 'CEL Seminar - Future Cities: Through Science, By Design, In Place, Over Time', '/cel-seminar-future-cities-through-science-by-design-in-place-over-time/', 'April 3rd, 2024 4:00pm Title: Future Cities: Through Science, By Design, In Place, Over Time Dr. Zhongming Shi is the Product Lead of the City Energy Analyst (CEA), an urban building energy simulation platform and one of the first open-source computational tool initiatives for the design of low-carbon and highly efficient cities. He owns CEA''s strategic direction of increasing education, professional practices, and business outreach. He is also teaching a studio-based course named “Integrate-design Project” at ETH Zurich. The course addresses urban design issues informed by building energy performance. Zhongming completed his PhD at the Future Cities Laboratory in Singapore. Then, he worked as the project coordinator at the Cities Knowledge Graph Project at the Singapore-ETH Centre. Meanwhile, he was the lead principal investigator for the project of building-integrated agriculture in collaboration with the Department of Architecture at the National University of Singapore. Categories: NEWS 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 October 2019 July 2019 May 2019 March 2019 June 2017 Categories NEWS Principle Investigator / Publications Uncategorized Meta Log in Entries feed Comments feed WordPress.org');
