INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('cel-seminar-rethinking-land-use-and-transport-interaction-some-behavioural-insights', 'CEL Seminar - Rethinking land-use and transport interaction – some behavioural insights', '/cel-seminar-rethinking-land-use-and-transport-interaction-some-behavioural-insights/', 'November 29th, 2023 11:00am-12:00pm Title: Rethinking land-use and transport interaction – some behavioural insights Dr Li Wan, Associate Professor in planning at the Department of Land Economy, University of Cambridge. He is the Director for the MPhil in Planning, Growth and Regeneration (PGR) programme and a Fellow of Gonville and Caius College. Dr Wan is interested in interdisciplinary modelling of urban land use and transport systems. Dr Li Wan is a co-investigator of the Centre for Smart Infrastructure and Construction and a Trustee of the IJURR Foundation. See projects of Dr Wan’s research group: liwan.work; also his new book: Digital Twins for Smart Cities (2023). Categories: NEWS 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 Dec