INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('collaborative-online-international-learning-between-shanghai-jiao-tong-university-and-seoul-national-university', 'Collaborative Online International Learning between Shanghai Jiao Tong University and Seoul National University', '/collaborative-online-international-learning-between-shanghai-jiao-tong-university-and-seoul-national-university/', 'Mar 18th - April 29th , 2024 Professor Quan, with Dr Hongdi He and Dr Hui Wang, held a ''Collaborative Online International Learning between Shanghai Jiao Tong University and Seoul National University''. Students who took ''Artificial Intelligence in Urban Planning and Design'' class which was designed to nascent applications of Al technologies in urban design and city planning, providing an overview of Al-based solutions. Students who joined these groups contributed to the interactive collaboration of the three assignments. Categories: Uncategorized 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 October 2019 July 2019 May 2019 March 2019 June 2017 Categories NEWS Principle Investigator / Publications Uncategorized Meta Log in Entries feed Comments feed WordPress.org');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('conference-city-energy-lab-at-the-2026-acsp-annual-conference', '[Conference] City Energy Lab at the 2026 ACSP Annual Conference', '/conference-city-energy-lab-at-the-2026-acsp-annual-conference/', '[Event Information] Event: 2026 Association of Collegiate Schools of Planning (ACSP) Annual Conference Location: Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, USA Date: October 2026 Presentation Title: Evaluating Cost-Effectiveness of Urban Heat Mitigation Strategies in Seoul’s Regeneration Projects Presenter: Sihyeon Kim, City Energy Lab, Seoul National University Award: JPER Top Reviewers Award (Dr. Steven Quan) Summary Sihyeon Kim, a master’s student at City Energy Lab, participated in the 2026 Association of Collegiate Schools of Planning (ACSP) Annual Conference held in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, USA. At the conference, she presented her research titled “Evaluating Cost-Effectiveness of Urban Heat Mitigation Strategies in Seoul’s Regeneration Projects.” The study examined the thermal performance and economic feasibility of urban heat mitigation strategies across different urban regeneration contexts in Seoul. Using ENVI-met simulations, the research evaluated three mitigation strategies—bright roofs, green roofs, and permeable pavements—across representative urban regeneration areas with distinct urban morphologies. The findings highlighted how the effectiveness and cost-efficiency of these strategies vary depending on local urban characteristics, emphasizing the importance of context-specific approaches to urban climate adaptation. In addition, Dr. Steven Quan was awarded the JPER Top Reviewers Award for Best Paper in the Journal of Planning Education and Research at the conference. The conference also provided opportunities to exchange research ideas with international scholars and discuss emerging approaches to urban climate resilience, sustainable urban planning, and data-driven urban analysis. Categories: Uncategorized 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 October 2019 July 2019 May 2019 March 2019 June 2017 Categories NEWS Principle Investigator / Publications Uncategorized Meta Log in Entries feed Comments feed WordPress.org');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('conference-city-energy-lab-at-the-7th-international-conference-on-environmental-design-and-health-iced-2026', '[Conference] City Energy Lab at the 7th International Conference on Environmental Design and Health (ICED 2026)', '/conference-city-energy-lab-at-the-7th-international-conference-on-environmental-design-and-health-iced-2026/', '[Event Information] Event: 7th International Conference on Environmental Design and Health (ICED 2026) Location: Harokopio University, Athens, Greece Dates: October 24–25, 2026 Oral Presentation: Implementing Artificial Intelligence-Enabled Participatory Planning Support Systems Presenter: Professor Steven Jige Quan, City Energy Lab, Seoul National University Session Chair: Professor Steven Jige Quan (Economics–Politics–Management–Social I) Poster Presentation: Quantifying Park Cooling Effects across Urban Contexts in Seoul: Using Geographically Weighted Gradient Boosting Decision Trees (GW-GBDT) Poster Presenter: Inseong Yum, City Energy Lab, Seoul National University Summary Professor Steven Jige Quan and Inseong Yum from City Energy Lab, Seoul National University, participated in the 7th International Conference on Environmental Design and Health (ICED 2026), held at Harokopio University in Athens, Greece, on October 24–25, 2026. At the conference, Professor Quan presented his research titled “Implementing Artificial Intelligence-Enabled Participatory Planning Support Systems,” co-authored with Seojung Lee. The study introduced a functional web-based platform integrating AI agents, a project-specific knowledge base, and generative AI tools to support five stages of participatory urban planning: problem definition, data analysis, alternative generation, alternative evaluation, and decision support. Using the Seoullo scenario as a demonstration, the research highlighted the potential of AI-enabled planning support systems to enhance stakeholder communication, information interpretation, and collaborative decision-making, while identifying practical challenges for real-world implementation. In addition to his presentation, Professor Quan served as the session chair for the Economics–Politics–Management–Social I session on October 24, facilitating academic presentations and discussions on environmental governance, policy, and sustainability. Inseong Yum delivered a poster presentation titled “Quantifying Park Cooling Effects across Urban Contexts in Seoul: Using Geographically Weighted Gradient Boosting Decision Trees (GW-GBDT),” co-authored with Professor Quan. Presented in the Cities poster session on October 25, the research explored spatial variations in urban park cooling effects across different urban contexts in Seoul, applying geographically weighted machine learning methods to investigate the relationship between urban environments and cooling performance. The conference provided opportunities to exchange research ideas with international scholars and discuss emerging approaches to AI-assisted participatory planning, urban climate resilience, and data-driven environmental design. Both presentations reflected City Energy Lab''s ongoing research efforts to advance sustainable and climate-responsive urban planning through computational and AI-based approaches. Categories: Uncategorized 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 20');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('conference-invited-talks-city-energy-lab-at-the-20th-international-association-for-china-planning-conference', '[Conference & Invited Talks] City Energy Lab at the 20th International Association for China Planning Conference', '/conference-invited-talks-city-energy-lab-at-the-20th-international-association-for-china-planning-conference/', '[Conference Information] • Conference: The 20th International Association for China Planning Conference • Organizer: International Association for China Planning • Location: Xi’an, China • Period: July 10–13, 2026 • Activities: Invited talks, conference presentations, and academic exchange Summary Professor Steven Jige Quan and members of the City Energy Lab attended the 20th International Association for China Planning Conference, held in Xi’an, China, from July 10 to 13, 2026. During the conference, Professor Quan delivered four presentations addressing major themes in contemporary urban planning, including climate resilience, global planning competencies, urban form analysis, and AI-enabled research. Lab members also presented their ongoing research and engaged in academic discussions with scholars and planning professionals from different institutions. The conference provided an opportunity for the lab to share its recent work, exchange ideas with the international planning community, and explore emerging research directions in sustainable urban development and artificial intelligence-assisted planning. Professor Quan’s Presentations • Urban Resilience, Climate Change, and Environmental Planning: Configuration, Electricity, and Emissions • Future Competencies and Global Engagement • Decoding Seoul’s Urban Form: From Latent Signals to Context-Grounded Archetypes • The Next Generation of Planning Research: AI-Enabled Research Automation and Human-AI Collaboration Lab Member’s Presentations • Heesoo Hwang — Standardizing Spatial Data for Urban AI: The Urban-Net Dataset • Inseong Yum — Understanding Park Cooling Effect Using ENVI-met: Considering Urban Context of Seoul • Lili Lin — Nonlinear Impacts of Urban Form on Urban Heat Islands: A Machine Learning Analysis Across Scales and Weather Conditions in Seoul • Seojung Lee — A Web-Based Implementation of an AI-Driven Participatory Planning Support System • Sihyeon Kim — Cost-Effective Heat Mitigation across Urban Regeneration Typologies: Implications for Urban Microclimate in Seoul • Subin Kim — Estimating Solar Energy Potential of Typical Regeneration Neighborhoods in Seoul • Yeqin Shen — Exploring the Spatially Heterogeneous Effects of Urban Form Factors on Urban Heat Island in Seoul Categories: Uncategorized 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 October 2019 July 2019 May 2019