INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('field-trip-2026-2-urban-planning-and-zoning-class', '[Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class', '/field-trip-2026-2-urban-planning-and-zoning-class/', 'On November 10, 2026, students from the Urban Planning and Zoning course at Seoul National University participated in a field trip to Seoul Forest and Seongsu-dong. The field trip aimed to explore urban regeneration, adaptive reuse of industrial buildings, and the relationship between zoning regulations and neighborhood transformation. The field trip began near Seoul Forest, followed by student presentations and discussions on the area''s urban development and planning characteristics. In the afternoon, participants explored Seongsu-dong, a former industrial district that has undergone significant transformation into a vibrant mixed-use neighborhood. The walking tour included Seongsu Handmade Shoe Street, Onion Seongsu, thisisneverthat HQ, Seoul Takju Brewery, Lezhin Comics Building, Seongsu Yeonbang, and Daelim Warehouse. These sites provided opportunities to examine the preservation of local manufacturing industries, the adaptive reuse of former factories, and architectural approaches to urban regeneration. In particular, students discussed how existing industrial structures and local building regulations have influenced the area''s evolving urban identity. Through on-site observations and discussions, students gained a deeper understanding of how urban planning policies, zoning, and architectural interventions interact in the regeneration of established urban neighborhoods. The field trip also highlighted the challenges of balancing heritage preservation, commercial development, and the continuity of local industries in rapidly changing urban environments. Categories: Uncategorized 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 October 2019 July 2019 May 2019 March 2019 June 2017 Categories NEWS Principle Investigator / Publications Uncategorized Meta Log in Entries feed Comments feed WordPress.org');
