INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('land-use-optimization-for-equitable-transit-oriented-development-case-study-of-austin-texas', 'CEL Seminar - Land Use Optimization for Equitable Transit Oriented Development: Case Study of Austin, Texas', '/land-use-optimization-for-equitable-transit-oriented-development-case-study-of-austin-texas/', '[City Energy Lab Lecture] City Energy Lab welcomes everyone from GSES to join a guest lecture. Speaker: Dr. Ming Zhang from The University of Texas at Austin Topic: Land Use Optimization for Equitable Transit Oriented Development: Case Study of Austin, Texas Time: August 11th, 2022 10:30 AM - 11:30 AMVenue: SNU GSES Building 82 Room 308 Short Bio: Dr. Ming Zhang is Professor and Program Director of Community & Regional Planning at the University of Texas at Austin and Director of the US DOT University Transportation Center of Cooperative Mobility for Competitive Megaregions (CM2). His research and teaching interests include urban and regional planning (transportation), the built environment-travel behaviour relationship, and GIS applications. His recent research has focused on megaregional transportation issues, Transit-Oriented Development, and high-speed rail and regional spatial development. Prior to joining UT Austin, Dr. Zhang held several academic and professional positions, including tenure-track Assistant Professor in the Department of Landscape Architecture & Urban Planning at Texas A&M University, Research Scientist at the Rockefeller Institute of Government in Albany, New York, and Lecturer at the Huazhong University of Science & Technology, Wuhan, China. Dr. Zhang received his B.Eng. and M.Eng. from Tsinghua University, Beijing and M.Sci. and Ph.D. from MIT, Cambridge, USA. Categories: NEWS 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 October 2019 July 2019 May 2019 March 2019 June 2017 Categories NEWS Principle Investigator / Publications Uncategorized Meta Log in Entries feed Comments feed WordPress.org');
