INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('na-li-parth-bansal-and-steven-jige-quan-published-an-article-in-sustainable-cities-and-society', 'Na Li, Parth Bansal and Steven Jige Quan published an article in Sustainable Cities and Society.', '/na-li-parth-bansal-and-steven-jige-quan-published-an-article-in-sustainable-cities-and-society/', 'Novemeber 2025 Na Li, Parth Bansal and Steven Jige Quan published an article in Sustainable Cities and Society. ''Thermal performance-based urban climate zone mapping through multivariate time series clustering: A case study of Seoul'' https://doi.org/10.1016/j.landusepol.2025.107878 Categories: Uncategorized 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 October 2019 July 2019 May 2019 March 2019 June 2017 Categories NEWS Principle Investigator / Publications Uncategorized Meta Log in Entries feed Comments feed WordPress.org');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('news', 'News', '/news/', '[Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class November 2026 Date: November 10, 2026 (Tuesday) Location: Seoul Forest and Seongsu-dong, Seoul, South Korea Participants: 12 students, teaching staff, and professor Course: Urban Planning and Zoning [Conference] City Energy Lab at the 7th International Conference on Environmental Design and Health (ICED 2026) October 2026 Professor Steven Jige Quan and Inseong Yum from City Energy Lab, Seoul National University, participated in the 7th International Conference on Environmental Design and Health (ICED 2026), held at Harokopio University in Athens, Greece. Professor Quan presented “Implementing Artificial Intelligence-Enabled Participatory Planning Support Systems” and served as the session chair for Economics–Politics–Management–Social I . Inseong Yum delivered a poster presentation titled “Quantifying Park Cooling Effects across Urban Contexts in Seoul: Using Geographically Weighted Gradient Boosting Decision Trees (GW-GBDT)” in the Cities poster session. [Event Information] • Event: 7th International Conference on Environmental Design and Health (ICED 2026) • Topics: Sustainability, Climate Change, Environmental Design, and Health • Location: Harokopio University, Athens, Greece • Dates: October 24–25, 2026 • Professor Quan: Oral Presentation and Session Chair (October 24) • Inseong Yum: Poster Presentation (October 25) [Online Conference] “Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul” October 2026 Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: “Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul”at the machine learning methods forum [Conference] City Energy Lab at the 2026 ACSP Annual Conference October 2026 Sihyeon Kim, a master’s student at City Energy Lab, participated in the 2026 Association of Collegiate Schools of Planning (ACSP) Annual Conference held in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, USA. [Event Information] • Event: 2026 Association of Collegiate Schools of Planning (ACSP) Annual Conference • Theme: Climate Resilience, AI in Planning, and Sustainable Urban Transformation • Location: Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, USA • Opening Date: October 8, 2026 [Guest Lecture] Seconds to Decades: High-Frequency Analytics to Low-Frequency Urban Design through Community-driven Digital Twins October 2026 . The City Energy Lab and the BK21 Four Program hosted Professor Perry Yang for the 254th GSES Colloquium on "Seconds to Decades: High-Frequency Analytics to Low-Frequency Urban Design through Community-driven Digital Twins. " [Event Information] • Speaker: Perry Yang, Professor • Affiliation: Georgia Institute of Technology • Date: October 15, 2026 • Time: 4:00–5:00 p.m. • Venue: SNU GSES Building 82, Room 113 [Publication] Multi-objective design optimization of educational buildings using CatBoost and NSGA-III under future climate scenarios September 2026 This study develops a multi-objective design optimization framework for educational buildings under future climate scenarios (2050 and 2080). By integrating CMIP6-based climate projections, CatBoost surrogate modeling, and NSGA-III, the study evaluates energy consumption, daylighting, and thermal comfort across three school building typologies. The CatBoost model accelerates simulations by approximately 180 times, while the optimization identifies window-to-wall ratio, building orientation, shading configuration, and wall materials as key design factors, supporting climate-adaptive and energy-efficient building design. [Publication Details] • Journal: Energy (2026) • Authors: Yeqin Shen, Steven Jige Quan, Yingnan Li, Waishan Qiu, Yuankai Wang, Junga Lee • DOI: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.energy.2026.141386 [Conference] Professor Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Septem');
