INSERT OR REPLACE INTO pages (slug, title, url, text) VALUES ('urban-informatics-a-trend-of-smart-planning-and-design', 'CEL Seminar - Urban Informatics: A Trend of Smart Planning and Design', '/urban-informatics-a-trend-of-smart-planning-and-design/', '[City Energy Lab Lecture (SNU) and Urban Design & Spatial Analysis Lab (HYU), AI-Aided and Data-Driven Design(AIDD) Lecture Series] City Energy Lab welcomes everyone from GSES to join a guest lecture. Speaker: Dr. Si Chen, visiting assistant professor in the Department of Geography, Texas A&M University Topic: Urban Informatics: Urban Informatics- A Trend of Smart Planning and Design Time: November 21th 2022, 11:00 AM – 12:00 PM (Seoul Time) Venue: Zoom lecture (https://snu-ac-kr.zoom.us/j/91823623444) Short Bio: Dr. Si Chen is a visiting assistant professor in the Department of Geography at Texas A&M University. Dr. Chen earned her Ph.D. in Urban Informatics through the Schools of Information Sciences at the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign, where she worked as a research assistant and associate director for the Landuse Evolution and impact Assessment Modeling Lab. She also obtained a Master of Computer Science and Master of Urban and Regional Planning from the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign. Her B.C. in Engineering was earned from the Department of Urban and Rural Planning and Design at Tongji University. Dr Chen’s research focuses on creating systems and methodologies that apply advanced data analytics to coupled urban and natural systems to support smart and sustainable development in the urban ecological context. Specific topics include urban informatics, spatial analysis, planning support system, accessibility, and sustainability. Dr. Chen has published multiple peer-reviewed journals on high-impact journals, such as Urban Forestry & Urban Greening, Travel Behaviour and Society, and Environment and Planning B: Urban Analytics and City Science . Categories: NEWS 0 Comments Leave a Reply Cancel reply Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked * Name * Email * Website What''s on your mind? Search for: Recent Posts [Field Trip] 2026-2 Urban Planning and Zoning Class The commencement day of Lili [Conference] Professor Steven Jige Quan at the 7th LH Global Business Convention (WSCE 2026) Professor Quan gave an online lecture on presentation title: "Examining Model Accuracy and Reliability of Explanations in Explainable Machine Learning for Urban Studies: A Case Study of Residential Building Energy Use in Seoul"at the machine learning methods forum Professor Quan delivered a lecture on "Explainable Machine Learning in Urban Research" at the Machine Learning Methods Forum at Chongqing University. Recent Comments ปั้มไลค์ on Joint Seminar with Hanyang University''s Urban Design and Spatial Analysis Lab Archives November 2026 September 2026 August 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 December 2025 September 2025 August 2025 June 2025 February 2025 January 2025 November 2024 October 2024 April 2024 March 2024 January 2024 October 2023 July 2023 May 2023 April 2023 February 2023 November 2022 August 2022 May 2022 April 2022 March 2022 December 2021 October 2021 August 2021 October 2019 July 2019 May 2019 March 2019 June 2017 Categories NEWS Principle Investigator / Publications Uncategorized Meta Log in Entries feed Comments feed WordPress.org');
